problem_statement:
`kv/service.py` serves reads through a cache, but `Service.update` writes only to the store, so `get` keeps returning the old value after an update. Fix this:

- add `Cache.invalidate(key)` in `kv/cache.py` (removing a missing key must not fail);
- `Service.update(key, value)` must make the next `get(key)` return the new value;
- add `Service.delete(key)`, which removes the key from the store and the cache; `get` of a deleted key returns None.

Add a dedicated exception for bad input:

- in `app/errors.py`, define `class ValidationError(AppError)`;
- `app/validators.py` currently raises ValueError in `check_age(age)` for ages outside 0-150; it must raise ValidationError instead;
- `app/api.py` has `handle(age)` that returns (200, "ok") for good input; it must return (400, <the error message>) when `check_age` raises ValidationError. Other exceptions must still propagate.
